@9010 = ~Missing Drow
Ulua, a drow at the Purple Wyrm Inn, has asked us to find her half-sister Vhaidra, who was last seen entering Baldur's Gate. We agreed to search the city for her.~
@9011 = ~Missing Drow
We found Vhaidra. The search for Ulua's missing half-sister is over, and the matter has been resolved.~
@9012 = ~Off with you, imbecile!~
@9013 = ~Have you found my sister? No? Then why are you still here?~
@9014 = ~Sss! Begone, rivvin. I have nothing to say to you.~
@9015 = ~Sss! Begone, rivvin. I have nothing to say to you.~
@9016 = ~You were the one staring. I caught a glimpse of that when I first walked in.~
@9017 = ~Why are you covering your face so m... oh, you're a dark elf.~
@9018 = ~Then I shall leave you be.~
@9019 = ~Sharp eyes. Make no mistake, I find your kind displeasing to be around. I thought you were someone else but since you aren't, leave!~
@9020 = ~Am I...? no! Absolutely not. I am merely a darkly tanned gold elf. I laid out too long on sparkling beaches of Evermeet. Now, farewell. Our conversation is over.~
@9021 = ~You do not recognise me, Viconia De'Vir? Because I recognised you immediately. Though it stuns me that you're among surface dwellers.~
@9022 = ~Hah! Still the snivelling bitch I see. Losing Lolth's favour must sting worse than mindthorn ever could.~
@9023 = ~Well, of course you'd say that. You've got your friends to cover behind if things go awry. Pathetic, but predictable. Once upon a time, House De'Vir was so dreaded and respected and it all went down to ashes. I surmise you experienced hatred, prejudice and racism wherever you went since the night you escaped the Underdark. Heh. Skipping forward, I came to this rotten sun-exposed hole not without a reason.~
@9024 = ~I'm pleased to see surface environment didn't erase your hardness and solidity. As much as my contempt for you goes, I always admired your tenacity and endurance. Don't fret. I am not here to hunt you down. If I had, you'd already lie in the pool of your own blood by now.~
@9025 = ~As a matter of fact, I may need temporary… allies. Your new toy here will do as I say, oh… with your permission, mistress De'Vir.~
@9026 = ~And offer your heart back to Lolth to gain privilege. Tempting. You are creative, Viconia. But no, I have no interest in sacrificing you. Hear me out.~
@9027 = ~House Uoswiir shared the same fate as yours, thought through different means. Once, we were the force to be reckoned with. Now, we are nothing but ashes and vestige of our former family. We've been wiped out.~
@9028 = ~Silence! I scorn pity, and would like nothing more than to avoid having it sent my way. We both ended up in similar situation. We were ruined by Dark Ravens - most lethal hidden society of assassins splintered from the order of Black Ravens. Monastic order of fools.~
@9029 = ~I already begun preparations to enact my revenge on them and avenge House Uoswiir and regrouped every surviving member to aid me. My 'outside' contacts also proven to be most valuable. Black Ravens will not escape my wrath.~
@9030 = ~Do not get feisty on me now, Viconia. My half-sister, Vhaidra… she survived the assault but I lost track of her. She was the target, whereas I was spared as monks considered my irrelevant in view of my bloodline. Vhaidra is the sole heir and legitimate scion of House Uoswiir. I need to find her if the operation is to be successful.~
@9031 = ~One of the unfortunate peasants that stood in my way provided me with plenty useful hints, suggesting that Vhaidra was last seen entering Baldur's Gate. Her tracks end here. While my henchmen are seeking the hideout of Dark Ravens, I need an outsider to thoroughly search the city for whereabouts of my half-sister.~
@9032 = ~So? Will you keep me waiting?~
@9033 = ~If I have the permission to speak for myself, sure. If that will put your mind at ease, we'll try to locate your half-sister.~
@9034 = ~It's beneath me to help someone like you.~
@9035 = ~Viconia, what do you think?~
@9036 = ~Only if I see a shiny gold coin heading my way.~
@9037 = ~I expected nothing less from underlings. I've been told Vhaidra was last seen somewhere close to Sorcerous Sundries. She could be anywhere now. Think, if you were a Drow, where would you hide.~
@9038 = ~Tsss! Moronic imbecile! You are in no position to undermine my authority! You're lucky we are within defenses of the city. Otherwise, I would personally make you gag on your own blood-soaking eyeballs! Now leave!~
@9039 = ~Affront! You are in no position to ask for reward. I am your better! Superior! You shall ask forgiveness at this very moment or else…~
@9040 = ~Or else what? We are in heavily fortified city with Flaming Fist, who openly despise your kind. Who do you think they will side with?~
@9041 = ~Vith dos, Iblith! I spit on your preponderance. I will find another servant to do my dirty work. You are of no use to me. Doer'ust!~
@9042 = ~What happened to my sister?~
@9043 = ~We found your sister. She attacked us and in turn we had no choice but to obliterate her.~
@9044 = ~You primitive, idiotic scoundrel. Iblith! I spit on you. Lolth will find and disintegrate you to ashes for this!~
@9045 = ~Oloth plynn dos... Look what crawls out of the Underdark and into a wretched surface tavern. Tell me, jalil, did your Matron Mother kick you out into the burning sun, or are you simply looking for a slave to put in chains? Careful <CHARNAME>, she wears familiar insignia on her. Can't quite put my finger on it yet.~
@9046 = ~Ulua of house Uoswiir from Menzoberranzan. How could I forget such a negligible, spoiled half-blood?~
@9047 = ~I shall not discuss my personal reasons with the likes of you, jalil. Besides, Baldur's Gate? Dangerous place for a lonely Drow traveller.~
@9048 = ~Spare me the exposition. I could not care less about your mission. We've got our own.~
@9049 = ~Charming.~
@9050 = ~And why would we do anything for you, Iblith. Our mutual history excludes cooperation, for obvious reasons and you don't exactly inspire trust. The second I turn my back, you'll stab me in it.~
@9051 = ~If you expect me to shed a tear over your sob story, I'll have to disappoint you.~
@9052 = ~Sounds like you got everything under control.~
@9053 = ~You're the leader so decision is ultimately yours, but assisting her may prove practical in effects. Drows aren't known for reliability and trustworthiness and Ulua can inform Lolth of my whereabouts. Accepting her request doesn't eradicate this risk. She could just backstab me. If we do not want to have Lolth's followers trailing us in the near future, it's a risk I believe we should take.~
@9054 = ~What do you want, rivvin?~
@9055 = ~What do you want, rivvin?~
@9056 = ~Spare me your sarcasm. I have no desire to fraternize with an obsolete Drow outcast. Especially you.~
@9057 = ~So?~
@9058 = ~Are you Vhaidra? Your sister, Ulua is looking for you.~
@9059 = ~Despicable that your kind is allowed entry here.~
@9060 = ~Ulua wants to see you back so you'll be coming with us.~
@9061 = ~Half-sister. Playing a worried sibling is unlike her. Touching that she cares. I'm assuming her revenge scheme plot is underway?~
@9062 = ~Splendid. I hadn't had much time to soil my hand in blood as of late. Killing Dark Ravens should prove beneficial in both satisfaction and vengeance field. I trust she found their location, pet?~
@9063 = ~We aren't her slaves or acolytes. We were just sent to find you.~
@9064 = ~I don't know, I don't care. Go to your sister so I can get this over with.~
@9065 = ~She's chosen her helpers well then. I like strong, disputatious and supercilious kind such as yourself. In her place, I'd take you to my bedchamber and make you beg for mercy... or beg for more.~
@9066 = ~Ulua? So she did survive the onslaught during the attack. How delightful. She found herself a delicious snack. In her place, I'd take you to my bedchamber and make you beg for mercy... or beg for more.~
@9067 = ~Enough building castles in the air. Where is my sister at?~
@9068 = ~Purple Wyrm Inn in eastern Baldur's Gate.~
@9069 = ~That information will cost you.~
@9070 = ~You've proven most useful as opposed to these blabbering fools occupying this city. Nothing but dobluth everywhere. I shall meet my sister. Vacate my chamber now.~
@9071 = ~And I was just going to grumble about how tedious it's been here.~
@9072 = ~Feisty piece of meat. Normally, I enjoy a little fight and chase, alas due to time constraints I must stick to the fight alone. Don't move... much.~
@9073 = ~Looks like I'll dirty my hands quicker than I anticipated. Wonderful.~
@9074 = ~Vhaidra Uoswiir. What an unpleasant surprise. This city has one drow too many.~
@9075 = ~Trust me, jalil. I pray that Shar will let me erase you from my memory once this meeting is over.~
@9076 = ~Carry on, jalil and you'll find your teeth on the floor. <CHARNAME>, we've done what we came here to do. Let's tarry no longer.~
